    "summary": "Blues‑heavy set with scorching Other One & blazing Hard to Handle",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blues‑laden first set that builds into an improvisational second half. Highlights include a fiery The Other One, a blistering Hard To Handle and a tight China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue. Jerry’s guitar soars while the rhythm section drives the jams.",
    "review": "December 12, 1970 at the Santa Rosa Fairgrounds captures the Dead in a gritty, blues‑focused mood that erupts into expansive jamming. The first set rolls through familiar terrain—Me And My Uncle, Truckin', and a heartfelt Brokedown Palace—before kicking up a notch with a scorching Hard To Handle and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition that showcases Bob’s solid rhythm work and a standout solo. \nThe second set dives deep into the band's improvisational well: Pigpen’s gritty “I’m A King Bee” sets a soulful tone, then the classic suite of Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One (despite a mid‑song splice) erupts with Jerry’s laser‑beam solos and soaring lead lines. From there the band rolls into an unbroken jam corridor—Darkness Jam, Saint Stephen Jam, and two takes of Good Lovin'—culminating in a jubilant Uncle John’s Band. While the soundboard source carries some hiss and occasional cuts, it remains clear enough to let Jerry’s crunchy tone and the tight interplay of Mickey and Billy shine through, making this recording the preferred listen for anyone wanting to experience this raw, high‑energy snapshot of the early ’70s Dead.",
